From 0181af9e44c3276d10a20ba87c6ad431b1efa314 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 12:35:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03257/11362] [outer-loop] arc submission: honest cap + recover
 2 graph-explore games (32 -> 34 offline-solid)

Two fixes after a parallel investigation of the submission path:

1. HONESTY (fixes a regression from fb7bff878): the live-submit driver sourced claimed levels
   from the package manifest (nominal 41), but the FLAT trajectory it actually replays reaches
   less for games whose deeper levels are reproduced-but-not-flat-banked (sc25 L5->L1, tu93 L5->L3,
   lp85 L5->L4). _build_claimed now CAPS each claim to the offline aggregate scorecard
   (results/arc3_replay_aggregate_scorecard.json -- what flat-replay truly reaches, OFFLINE/zero
   quota) and surfaces the capped games at validate time. The driver can no longer over-claim.

2. RECOVERY (+2 levels): dc22 and vc33 were dropped (no GAME_ARTIFACTS pointer) despite having a
   replayable banked trajectory on disk (dc22 under "solution", vc33 under "trajectory"; both
   load_actions/normalize-clean, both reproduce L1 offline). Registered them in the metaharness.
   Offline aggregate confirmed 32 -> 34 levels / 16 -> 18 games, zero network.

Honest submittable floor is now 34 levels (was a 39 over-claim) vs the 13-level 2026-06-17
baseline = +21. Deferred ft09 (conductor .421 A4 deepen target -- file-race on arc_game_adapters.py);
treated ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml read-only (conductor-written this milestone). Submission stays
operator-only: validate-first surfaces live env-mismatch before any irreversible close. 4 tests green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
